<BaseLayout locale="en" title="Privacy · GenshinPiano"><section class="page-hero shell"><span class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</span><h1>Privacy and network access</h1><p>We aim to keep your data on your computer and make network activity transparent and controllable.</p></section><section class="section shell"><article class="legal"><h2>Website</h2><p>This site has no account system, comment form, or behavioral profiling. It is hosted by GitHub Pages, so visits may be subject to GitHub's own logs and privacy policy.</p><h2>Local app data</h2><p>Scores, settings, logs, update caches, and OCR add-ons are stored in the application folder. Review logs for local paths or score names before sharing them.</p><h2>Network features</h2><p>The app can connect to GitHub or GitCode to check for updates and download packages or the OCR add-on. Network access, automatic updates, and preview releases are controlled under Settings → Updates.</p><h2>Game input</h2><p>Performance uses local Windows input APIs only after you start playback and while a supported game window is focused. The app does not collect account credentials.</p><h2>Third-party music</h2><p>Scores may transcribe or arrange existing works. The MIT License for the software does not grant rights to third-party music, names, or assets.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>For privacy or project questions, contact us through <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/tozyx/GenshinPiano/issues">GitHub Issues</a>.</p></article></section></BaseLayout>